// A known limitation (the CIL frontend translation, §12.3): the index admits a path only if a
// statement spells it or a chain of loads in one block builds it. Storing an object whose own
// field was stored earlier does neither: after `n.g = x; o.f = n`, `o.f.g <- x` holds, but no
// statement spells `.f.g`, so the index derives no such summary. `cil:taint` meets this in
// `Exec.Obj::ObjectField` (`b.O = new Node { Value = a }; return b.O`); its known-miss file
// points here. `flowy_tests.rs` skips this file until the index composes such paths.
def F(o, x)
where summaries [o.f.g <- x]
{
start:
  n.g = x;
  o.f = n;
  return;
}
